## 2. Where Proxy API Calls Are Made (HTTP Layer)

### 2.1 The Core HTTP Client

**File**: `/Users/admin/project/integrated-search/outbound/client/proxy-api/src/main/kotlin/com/cowave/search/client/proxy_api/ProxyApiClient.kt`

```kotlin
@Component
class ProxyApiClient(
    @field:Qualifier("ProxyHttpGraphQlClient")
    private val client: HttpGraphQlClient  // Spring GraphQL WebClient
) {
    fun <T> query(
        query: String,              // GraphQL query string
        variables: Map<String, Any> = emptyMap(),
        retrievePath: String,       // JSON path to extract data
        classType: Class<T>,
    ): List<T> {
        return try {
            client.document(query)
                .variables(variables)
                .retrieveSync(retrievePath)  // Synchronous call
                .toEntityList(classType)
        } catch (ex: Exception) {
            logger.error { ex }
            throw ex
        }
    }
}
```

**Configuration**:
```kotlin
@Bean("ProxyHttpGraphQlClient")
fun httpGraphQlClient(): HttpGraphQlClient {
    return HttpGraphQlClient.builder(WebClient.create(prop.baseUrl))
        .headers { it.setBasicAuth(prop.username, prop.password) }
        .build()
}
```

**Properties** (`application-outbound.yml`):
